.png\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/69c3f9e80170c.png\"><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/69c3f9e8231dc.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/69c3f9e8231dc.jpg\"></a><br>- sottile / nitida (probabilmente coniata a Kremnica, in Slovacchia).</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/69c3f9cd940cf.png\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/69c3f9cd940cf.png\"></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/69c3f9dbec808.png\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/69c3f9dbec808.png\"></a></p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">I colpi di Kremnica tendono ad avere un bordo più spesso e colpi più definiti e nitidi, mentre i colpi di Sofia tendono ad avere un bordo sottile o appena percettibile e colpi più indefiniti e sfocati.<br><br></p>","tags":["Altri animali","Cavallo o equino","Carta geografica"],"weight":7.8,"orientation":"medal","edge":{"description":"Rientrato","picture":"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/photos/bulgarie/6a09cd6d0f7895.91852552-original.jpg","thumbnail":"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/photos/bulgarie/6a09cd6d0f7895.91852552-180.jpg","picture_copyright":"Renato Lima","picture_license_name":"CC BY-NC","picture_license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/deed.it"},"mints":[{"id":1329,"name":"Bulgarian Mint"},{"id":1262,"name":"Kremnica"}],"category":"coin","type":"Moneta di circolazione regolare"}}